# Spatial AI for Urban Traffic Congestion Analysis

This project explores how geospatial data and unsupervised machine learning can be used to identify and interpret urban traffic congestion patterns.

Real-time traffic flow data from the HERE Traffic API is combined with OpenStreetMap roadway data and analyzed using K-Means clustering. Traffic conditions are compared between peak and off-peak periods in downtown San Francisco using congestion metrics, roadway classifications, and spatial characteristics.

## Workflow

1. Retrieve real-time traffic flow data from the HERE Traffic API
2. Construct and enrich roadway data using OpenStreetMap and OSMnx
3. Engineer congestion and spatial features
4. Standardize features for machine learning
5. Apply and evaluate unsupervised clustering methods
6. Classify roadway segments by congestion level
7. Compare peak and off-peak traffic conditions
8. Visualize spatial patterns using Folium
9. Summarize model outputs for interpretation

